
<p class="lead">Your syllabus is more than a list of dates and policies&mdash;it&rsquo;s an invitation to learning, a tool for transparency, and a foundation for building an inclusive, student-centered classroom. The Center for Teaching and Learning encourages faculty to design syllabi that clearly communicate expectations and foster a sense of belonging from day one. Below, you will find the university&rsquo;s syllabus requirements and resources to help you create a document that not only meets policy but also inspires student engagement and success.</p>

